From: Brian Cain <brian.cain@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gallium: fix pipe_transfer usage bitfield width on hexagon

pipe_transfer::usage is declared as a 24-bit bitfield of type
'enum pipe_map_flags'. On most targets the compiler picks a 4-byte
underlying type for a plain enum, but the Hexagon ABI picks the
smallest unsigned integer type that fits all enumerators (here 16
bits, since the largest enumerator is 1<<14). That makes the 24-bit
bitfield wider than its own underlying type, which Clang rejects:

  error: width of bit-field 'usage' (24 bits) exceeds the width of
  its type (16 bits)

Use a plain unsigned bitfield instead, matching the neighboring
pipe_resource::usage field which already avoids the enum type for
the same reason.

Signed-off-by: Brian Cain <brian.cain@gmail.com>
---
 src/gallium/include/pipe/p_state.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/include/pipe/p_state.h b/src/gallium/include/pipe/p_state.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/gallium/include/pipe/p_state.h
+++ b/src/gallium/include/pipe/p_state.h
@@ -619,7 +619,7 @@
 struct pipe_transfer
 {
    struct pipe_resource *resource; /**< resource to transfer to/from  */
-   enum pipe_map_flags usage:24;
+   unsigned usage:24;              /**< PIPE_MAP_x bitmask */
    unsigned level:8;               /**< texture mipmap level */
    struct pipe_box box;            /**< region of the resource to access */
    unsigned stride;                /**< row stride in bytes */
